  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">R&#xE9;ponse holistique aux besoins des communaut&#xE9;s affect&#xE9;es par les VBG, bas&#xE9;e sur une approche participative et inclusive de renforcement de la r&#xE9;silience des femmes et des filles dans les communes cibles du projet</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of UNFPA project is to improve the quality of services and access to information to prevent people from exposing to gender-based violence and take effective care of the victims who suffered from GBV in four flagship communes in the Tillab&#xE9;ry and Diffa regions. The project provides awareness campaigns and information sessions about GBV in the targeted communities, essential medical, psychosocial and legal support, socio-recreational activities, support to start income-generating vocational activities and the establishment of GBV working groups at commune level. The intervention provides humanitarian assistance to 9,500 people (95 men, 4,275 women and 5,130 children), including 285 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
